0764,\n","         17.55483543,  18.37906322,  19.20329102,  20.02751881,\n","         20.8517466 ,  21.67597439,  22.50020218]),\n"," <BarContainer object of 50 artists>)"]},"metadata":{},"execution_count":26},{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["<Figure size 640x480 with 1 Axes>"],"image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}],"source":["plt.hist(hpreact.view(-1).tolist(), 50)"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"3MGnKfkRy45D"},"source":["- Notice the broadness of the distribution. This is why a lot of numbers are being squashed and capped after a `tanh`, and lots of them take on extreme values.\n","\n","<u>**This means the distribution is too saturated.**</u>\n","\n","<u>**They update less frequently.**</u>\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"7Yn4ydVezLXE"},"source":["### !! Issue - Broad h value (Important: Dead Neurons)"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"KjZGYMZ0znEh"},"source":["- During backpropagation, we start at the loss, through the network, backwards. Note on:\n","\n","`h = torch.tanh(hpreact)`\n","\n","has 200 neurons, and implements activation function of `tanh`. From `Part 1 - Micrograd`. Notice:"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"ExRJOrxW09J9"},"source":["![image.png](data:image/png;base64,)"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"FpRxXmHy097A"},"source":["- The backpropagation of tanh, in this implementation, is the `1-t^2`, then multiply it with the local gradient `out.grad`.\n"," - If `t= 1, self.grad = 0 * out.grad` - tanh squash the gradient - destroyed\n"," - If `t=-1, self.grad = 0 * out.grad` - tanh squash the gradient - destroyed\n"," - If `t= 0, self.grad = 1 * out.grad` - tanh becomes inactive    - vanished\n","\n","At `self.grad = 0`\n","- Effectively, <u>the gradient is killed and `out.grad` **stop changing**</u>.\n","- If the output is close to `-1.0` or `1.0`, the output is at the tail of the `tanh` function, <u>thus changing the input will not affect the output of tanh because it is at the flat region of tanh, loss is not impacted</u>.\n","- The weights and biases along with this `tanh` neuron do not impact the loss, because the output of this tanh unit is in the flat region of the tanh, there is no influence.\n","\n","- AKA the neurons in -1 are permanently minimally influencing the output - neuron never learns, destroyed neuron.\n","- AKA the neurons in  1 are permanently maximally influencing the output -\n","neuron never learns, destroyed neuron.\n","- AKA the neurons in  0 are just passing through.\n","- `tanh` can only decrease gradients proportional to where the numbers are in the graph and how far it is from the flat lines.\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":27,"metadata":{"id":"9IKDdKKO2PN_","colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":472},"executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1744009665449,"user_tz":-480,"elapsed":172,"user":{"displayName":"JoyceL U","userId":"15152067095379831731"}},"outputId":"338a4628-33e0-43fa-f64c-10c4b9ccd65e"},"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["<Figure size 640x480 with 1 Axes>"],"image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}],"source":["import numpy as np\n","x_values = np.linspace(-5, 5, 400)\n","y_values = np.tanh(x_values)\n","\n","plt.plot(x_values, y_values, label='tanh(x)')\n","plt.title('Plot of the Hyperbolic Tangent Function')\n","plt.xlabel('x')\n","plt.ylabel('tanh(x)')\n","plt.legend()\n","plt.show()"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"kzTAqq5L5s3Y"},"source":["Let us see absolute value of H, and see how often it is to be in the flat regions."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":28,"metadata":{"id":"gH66_ede510x","colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":328},"executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1744009665652,"user_tz":-480,"elapsed":201,"user":{"displayName":"JoyceL U","userId":"15152067095379831731"}},"outputId":"8d070d10-bd0b-4cd2-ae97-82f847d3a4dd"},"outputs":[{"output_type":"execute_result","data":{"text/plain":["<matplotlib.image.AxesImage at 0x7a798df8d550>"]},"metadata":{},"execution_count":28},{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["<Figure size 2000x1000 with 1 Axes>"],"image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}],"source":["plt.figure(figsize=(20,10))\n","plt.imshow(h.abs() > 0.99, cmap='gray', interpolation='nearest')"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"XAqQptWG8Gfw"},"source":["Luckily non of the neurons in this model is dead, although there is a lot of whites. All the neurons are still somewhat functional albeit not optimal."]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"v56Jay9G6AoI"},"source":["- `h.abs() > 0.99,` is a Boolean tensor\n","  - White dot = `True`\n","  - Black dot = `False`\n","- Black dots are when its not in flat region.\n","- White dots are in flat tail - destroyed gradients\n","\n","<u>Note: If you see a whole column of white - it is called `dead neuron`</u>\n","- Dead neuron\n"," - Initialization of W&B could be such that no single example ever activates the tanh function.\n"," - If all examples land in the tail of tanh, Neuron no longer learns, it is a dead neuron.\n"," - Whenever you pass in any input, this neuron will always output `1.0` or `-1.0`, and it never learns because the gradient will just become `0`."]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"RU9A8ckF8lRF"},"source":["#### Note - Nonlinear AFuncs with Squashing neurons\n","\n","- Activation Functions with squashing neuron will have this same issue\n"," - Sigmoid\n"," - Tanh\n"," - ReLU - Flat below 0.0 - Preactivate below `0.0` becomes `0.0`, gradients will also be set `=0.0`, neuron never learn.\n","\n","- Note: Dead neuron can happen at initialization or at optimization.\n","- Note: Overly large learning rate may cause dead neurons!"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"_rlBnfPj_reJ"},"source":["### Solution - Fixing saturated tanh"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"93JBT6Ut_4MM"},"source":["This is first batch - initialization:\n","\n","Summary of issues:\n","- `hpreact = embcat @ W1 + b1` - h pre-activation is too large (too far off from 0)\n","  - `embcat` is from C table, a uniform Gaussian\n","  -  We want this variable to be closer to 0, similar to logits, W2 and b2."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":29,"metadata":{"id":"UT3p8fbr_wHp","colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1744009665659,"user_tz":-480,"elapsed":6,"user":{"displayName":"JoyceL U","userId":"15152067095379831731"}},"outputId":"23a93624-bf31-48be-eda5-cb1def93e6f1"},"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["11897\n"]}],"source":["# MLP Revisited\n","n_embd = 10 # Dimensionality of character embedding vectors\n","n_hidden = 200 # Number of neurons in hidden layer of MLP\n","\n","g = torch.Generator().manual_seed(2147483647)\n","C = torch.randn((vocab_size, n_embd), generator=g)\n","W1 = torch.randn((n_embd*block_size, n_hidden), generator=g)  * 0.2\n","b1 = torch.randn(n_hidden,                      generator=g)  * 0.01\n","W2 = torch.randn((n_hidden,vocab_size),         generator=g)  * 0.01\n","b2 = torch.randn(vocab_size,                    generator=g)  * 0\n","\n","parameters = [C, W1, b1, W2, b2]\n","print(sum(p.nelement() for p in parameters))\n","for p in parameters:\n","  p.requires_grad = True"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":30,"metadata":{"id":"4z7812Cx_zlz","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1744009666217,"user_tz":-480,"elapsed":549,"user":{"displayName":"JoyceL U","userId":"15152067095379831731"}}},"outputs":[],"source":["emb = C[Xtr] # (32, 3, 2)\n","h = torch.tanh(emb.view(-1, 30) @ W1 + b1) # (32, 100)\n","logits = h @ W2 + b2\n","loss = F.cross_entropy(logits, Ytr)"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":31,"metadata":{"id":"1yPJGLXG_26_","colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1744009666222,"user_tz":-480,"elapsed":3,"user":{"displayName":"JoyceL U","userId":"15152067095379831731"}},"outputId":"83296fc5-6816-421a-f5a1-e5086cbe520d"},"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["      0/  10000: 3.3135\n"]}],"source":["# Same optimization as last time\n","# max_steps = 200000\n","max_steps = 10000\n","batch_size = 32\n","lossi = []\n","\n","for i in range(max_steps):\n","\n","  # Minibatch construct\n","  ix = torch.randint(0, Xtr.shape[0], (batch_size,), generator=g)\n","  Xb, Yb = Xtr[ix], Ytr[ix] # Batch X,Y\n","\n","  # Forward pass\n","  emb = C[Xb] # Embed characters into vectors\n","  embcat = emb.view(emb.shape[0], -1) # Concatenate the vectors\n","  hpreact = embcat @ W1 + b1 # Hidden layer pre-activation\n","  h = torch.tanh(hpreact) # Hidden layer\n","  logits = h @ W2 + b2 # Output layer\n","  loss = F.cross_entropy(logits, Yb) # Loss function\n","\n","  # Backward pass\n","  for p in parameters:\n","    p.grad = None\n","  loss.backward()\n","\n","  # Update\n","  lr = 0.1 if i < 100000 else 0.01 # Step learning rate decay\n","  for p in parameters:\n","    p.data += -lr * p.grad\n","\n","  # Track stats\n","  if i % 10000 == 0: # Print\n","    print(f'{i:7d}/{max_steps:7d}: {loss.item():.4f}')\n","  lossi.append(loss.log10().item())\n","  break"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":32,"metadata":{"id":"K9Zo-QMNA4qP","colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":734},"executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1744009666418,"user_tz":-480,"elapsed":197,"user":{"displayName":"JoyceL U","userId":"15152067095379831731"}},"outputId":"17f3ef75-4c0a-429e-8b44-4ec73e2627c9"},"outputs":[{"output_type":"execute_result","data":{"text/plain":["(array([  1.,   2.,   0.,   1.,   5.,   3.,  11.,   6.,  13.,  10.,  25.,\n","         40.,  40.,  77.,  63., 101., 127., 171., 184., 220., 227., 267.,\n","        312., 301., 356., 367., 376., 360., 370., 331., 298., 278., 292.,\n","        242., 191., 167., 137., 104.,  85.,  77.,  41.,  30.,  28.,  20.,\n","         11.,   7.,  11.,   5.,   2.,   7.]),\n"," array([-3.76367092, -3.62009715, -3.476